      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, I want to leave this as-is and then after a follow-up in https://pdfium-review.googlesource.com/c/pdfium/+/135730/4/core/fxcodec/png/skia_png_decoder.h:\n\n1. If `progressive_decoder.cpp` includes `core/fxcodec/png/libpng_png_decoder.h` (this file) then we will have `PngDecoder \u003d LibpngPngDecoder`\n2. If `progressive_decoder.cpp` includes `core/fxcodec/png/skia_png_decoder.h` (from the follow-up CL) then we will have `PngDecoder \u003d SkiaPngDecoder`\n\nThis kind of duck-typing is fairly straightforward and works here.\n\nIn theory I could also introduce an abstract `PngDecoderBase` class with `StartDecode` and `ContinueDecode` methods.  I didn\u0027t do this, because changing `static` methods into `virtual` methods felt bit weird - it wasn\u0027t clear to me who would 1) construct a specific kind of decoder and 2) what would be the lifetime of the decoder (e.g. would `PngDecoder::ContinueDecode(...)` change to `CreatePngDecoder().ContinueDecode(...)` VS would results of `CreatePngDecoder` be stored in a field of `progressive_decoder.cpp` or in a static-or-global variable somewhere)?\n\nAny feedback?",
      "parentUuid": "0a4a2ac8_264211ea",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 39,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 39,
        "endChar": 16
